== Play as the space-between: Conceptualization

Play marks the space in which conceptualization takes place; it is the ground
upon which the rules are made, upon which differentiation occurs. It is the body
without organs, it is the space of différance. It is the space in Sassurean
semiotics in which conceptualization opens up, _between words_ so to speak; the
space of meaning-making in the distinction between words, their meaning only
occurring through the entire net of symbolic representation (Quine's network of
beliefs). Derrida considers it both "temporizing" and "spacing"
#cite(<Derridadifferancebasspdf>). Play is the free movement of the psyche
within the rigid conceptualization of the symbolic order. The unconscious moves
freely and finds resistances in the structure of symbols. The aesthetic revvs up
the engines, in Kant's sense, and gets the play moving. It confronts us with new
ideas and ways of symbolizing, it shakes up the symbolic order, pushing at its
boundaries until something comes loose and we re-conceptualize.
